@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #0b7a75
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9ca3af

title One release, and which of its three gates actually hold

left to right direction

rectangle "operator\nintent" as OP
rectangle "GATE 1\nhuman presence" as G1 #fdf6f6
rectangle "approval\nrecord" as AR
rectangle "GATE 2\nthe record itself" as G2 #fdf6f6
rectangle "migration\nservice" as MS
rectangle "GATE 3\nappend-only role" as G3 #f2f9f5
rectangle "serve\nstore" as SS

OP -right-> G1
G1 -right-> AR
AR -right-> G2
G2 -right-> MS
MS -right-> G3
G3 -right-> SS

note bottom of G1
  BROKEN. The proof of a human is a value the
  requesting process supplies. Whoever asks can
  say a person was present.
end note

note bottom of G2
  BROKEN. The releasing identity holds INSERT on
  the collection that carries its own release
  authorisation. It can write its own permission.
end note

note bottom of G3
  HOLDS. No update, no delete, no drop. The
  server refuses, whatever the code asks.
end note

note as FOOT #fff4e5
  Two of three gates are CHECKS: they ask the actor
  a question and believe the answer.
  One is an INCAPACITY: the actor cannot do the thing,
  so there is nothing to ask.

  Adopt the incapacity first.
end note
@enduml
